{"id": "EUVD-2026-103856", "enisaUuid": "de3b10ac-1f7a-35b9-b1d6-b222f3770f7d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: storage: sierra_ms: reject short SWoC info transfers\n\nsierra_get_swoc_info() requests sizeof(struct swoc_info) (60) bytes\nfrom the device via usb_control_msg(), but its callers only treat a\nnegative return value as failure. A device that answers the\nvendor-specific GetSwocInfo request with a short IN transfer is\ntherefore accepted, leaving the tail of the freshly allocated\n(kmalloc(), non-zeroing) swoc_info buffer uninitialized.\n\ntruinst_show() subsequently prints swocInfo->rev, swocInfo->LinuxSKU\nand swocInfo->LinuxVer from that buffer into the world-readable\n(0444) \"truinst\" sysfs attribute. An emulated/malicious USB device\n(VID 0x1199, PID 0x0fff) can exploit this to disclose up to 5 bytes\nof stale kernel heap memory (kmalloc-64) to unprivileged userspace,\nonce per sysfs read, indefinitely. On kernels built without\ninit_on_alloc this leaks recently freed heap contents.\n\nOnly accept the transfer when the full structure was received.\nsierra_ms_init() already retries failed queries, so well-behaved\ndevices are unaffected.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:46", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4faaad69f18332246bbd4ca41718beb2a305bb72", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c85e8331d298b8f1dee8fe63718e76435cec7133", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e2d62928f2666a2964a23b1d39e6e762f0628d7b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/db9d3be156baca6ef80ae5d93acfeb85c61a74dd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a0200d14acd9db388b85cd016e68a4e60d900ec"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7hw4-87pj-mc7h", "CVE-2026-98771"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "152b9d3b-3125-3e7a-93a3-1b4825ef47fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "1913baab-cd3a-3fc0-988a-bf2bd215f290", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "33b11f65-5550-30b6-94be-50b407646fce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "32fe5e393455d87db4988af03915634304870fb4 <c85e8331d298b8f1dee8fe63718e76435cec7133"}, {"id": "5be3f003-862d-3da2-8d1f-b62d5051868b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "32fe5e393455d87db4988af03915634304870fb4 <db9d3be156baca6ef80ae5d93acfeb85c61a74dd"}, {"id": "79a95125-b5d2-357e-ac99-7cc0b700ad11", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8e14a449-da52-321f-91da-9d5e381fb77f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.27"}, {"id": "9479eda7-8727-3658-8f34-c3f90379d292", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "956c274e-48a5-3895-81ca-bf36f94f498b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "32fe5e393455d87db4988af03915634304870fb4 <e2d62928f2666a2964a23b1d39e6e762f0628d7b"}, {"id": "c20ce295-912c-3343-90cb-527bc7706916", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "32fe5e393455d87db4988af03915634304870fb4 <8a0200d14acd9db388b85cd016e68a4e60d900ec"}, {"id": "cebcb653-0f69-3cb7-b024-9b6363d56e91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "d76c9623-de0b-3512-b531-92fae9f25a3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "fcd67618-536d-3f2f-ae5f-8df4883c512a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "32fe5e393455d87db4988af03915634304870fb4 <4faaad69f18332246bbd4ca41718beb2a305bb72"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e5afe4b9-f7f6-3688-8099-c4e5a02f6a1f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false